-------------------------------------------The starred programs -- what they need and where they are------------------------------------------------------There used to be a /dd/CMDS/NEEDCIO directory holding these apart.  It isgone: they now sit in /dd/CMDS and /dd/CMDS/GAMES with everything else, andthe star before the name is what tells them apart.  That is deliberate --sorting a collection by which libraries its author happened to link againsthelps nobody browse it.Each was compiled `cc -qixm`: the C library lives in Microware's `cio` traphandler rather than being linked in, which made for small binaries and wasthe normal way to build for OS-9.  `cio`, `csl` and `math` are licensedpart of Microware's OS-9 SDK.  They are not in this collection -- if you runOS-9 you have them already, and DOC/README-CIO shows how to point at them.DOC/README-CIO explains the three ways to set this up.All 107, verified by running every program on this disk with no cio present:  aprocs        as09          autolf        back          basename.cio  bm            cal           cat.cio       cb            ccheck  chbase        checkenv      chgrp         chown         ci  ckermit       co            cp            cribbage      cxref  delbak        detab         dir           dirname.cio   divide  dm            dmake         dpark         ed            edir  emacs         emacs.mm1     ephem         ephem881      eset  eunlink       exist         expand        fc            fgrep  field         forth         gawk          gdd           getenv  gnuchess      gnuchessn     gnuchessr     gnuplot       head  hotel         initvdu       ksh           l             larn  launch        loglist       lua           luac          mexist  mg            mille         mkdir         move          mv  owner         paranoia      perr          piano         printenv  psc           qsort9        rcs           rcsdiff       rcsident  rcsmerge      rechne        rlog      