to /dd/tmp.Hardcoded /h0 paths were NOT all rewritten -- 108 programs stillcarry one. 70 of them look for /h0/sys/termcap and 50 for data oftheir own (hack wants /h0/games/hack/playground, cribbage wants/h0/games/crib/criblog). The fix is to give os9exec the same imagetwice, as /dd and as /h0:    OS9DISK=<this disk>  OS9H0=<this disk>  os9exec ...OS-9 filenames are case-insensitive, so /h0/games/hack/playgroundfinds GAMES/HACK/playground. Verified: hack fails without it andstarts with it.THERE IS NO SNOBOL INTERPRETER HERE, and none is missing.  Sevenprograms used to be described as a "SNOBOL demo", which sent peoplelooking for a language that was never part of this.  They are RobertHeller's SNOBOL4-in-C: a C library that simulates SNOBOL4's patternmatcher, with programs translated out of Gimpel's "Algorithms inSNOBOL4".  Each is an ordinary 68k program that needs nothing else.The library and its makefile are in SRC/effo_snobol, the package's ownnotes in DOC/snobol.  blackjak, poker, rpoem, rstory, rstory2, stoneand tformat are the seven.larn resolves the same way: it wants /h0/GAMES/larn/PLAYGROUND, andGAMES/LARN/PLAYGROUND is on the disk.  It holds the scoreboard larnwrites there for itself, plus .larn.help, .lfortune and .larnmaze.larn plays, and the in-game '?' help works -- verified: it lays outa level, shows its help, keeps score and takes commands.Those three data files came from the larn 12.2p4 sources, not from12.0, which is the version this binary reports.  No 12.0 source hassurvived that we can find.  SOURCES.txt records where they camefrom.  Its sibling ularn is complete and also runs.  gnuchessc andgnuan used to fail for want of data; theirs has since beenrecovered into GNUCHESS4.0/MISC and both now start.DOC/DEPENDS lists, per program, every absolute path its binarycarries -- read it before copying single commands elsewhere.See DOC/REBUILT-NOTES.md for four curated binaries that wereoverwritten during installati